I think the idea is that a language needs ordinary terms for species (ie. w=
ords like =93bullfinch=94, not words like =93Pyrrhula pyrrhula=94). In the =
cases were a gismu is not adequate, a new word needs to be created, and the=
 word needs to come from somewhere. Often, the scientific name is an easily=
 available source to make a new word from. That doesn't mean that the new w=
ord is a _translation_ or _corresponds with_ or _is used the same way as_ t=
he Linnean binomial, just that it's based on that term, rather than a word =
from some particular language.

